      ],
      "solution": "$\\int x e^{x^2+2}\\,dx = \\int e^u \\times \\frac{1}{2}\\frac{du}{dx}\\,dx\\quad \\left\\{u = x^2+2 \\implies \\frac{du}{dx} = 2x\\right\\} = \\int \\frac{1}{2}e^u\\,du = \\frac{1}{2}e^u + c = \\frac{1}{2}e^{x^2+2} + c$",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "Integration by substitution for exponential functions of the form $f'(x)e^{f(x)}$.",
