      "solution": "$\\int \\frac{e^{\\frac{1}{x}}}{x^2}\\,dx = \\int e^u\\left(-\\frac{du}{dx}\\right)dx\\quad \\left\\{u = \\frac{1}{x} \\implies \\frac{du}{dx} = -\\frac{1}{x^2}\\right\\} = \\int -e^u\\,du = -e^u + c = -e^{\\frac{1}{x}} + c$",
